RUNZE RP42 Industrial Micro Syringe Pump 

 The RUNZE RP42 is a compact industrial micro Syringe pump for precise aspiration and dispensing in analytical instruments and automated fluid systems. Available in 100, 500 and 1000 uL capacities, it supports integrated-driver and external-drive configurations for OEM equipment integration. 
































































 Send Mail 


 Share this product:




























 Product OverviewThe RUNZE RP42 is a compact industrial micro Syringe pump designed for precise aspiration and dispensing in analytical instruments, laboratory equipment and automated fluid systems. A stepper motor and lead-screw transmission convert rotary motion into controlled Syringe travel for stable micro-volume fluid handling.The series is available in 100, 500 and 1000 uL capacities. Integrated-driver versions support RS-232 and RS-485 communication with RUNZE, MODBUS and ASCII protocols. External-drive versions provide optocoupler home-position sensing for OEM controller integration.Dual 10-32 UNF Syringe wash ports can be connected to a cleaning circuit to help remove deposits from the ceramic Syringe surface. The transparent PCTG pump head allows visual inspection of the fluid path during setup and maintenance.Key Features• Volume error <=1% at rated stroke.• Repeatability error of 0.3%-0.7% at rated stroke.• 100, 500 and 1000 uL capacity options.• Minimum dispense resolution from 0.025 uL, depending on capacity and lead-screw pitch.• Dual Syringe wash ports help reduce crystal build-up and maintenance frequency.• PCTG, alumina ceramic, UPE and FKM wetted materials.• RS-232 and RS-485 communication on integrated-driver versions.• RUNZE, MODBUS and ASCII control protocols.• Tested for 3,000,000 cycles without leakage using pure water at one rated stroke per cycle.Technical Specifications• Nominal volume: 100 uL / 500 uL / 1000 uL• Back pressure: 0.5 MPa• Rated stroke: 12.7 mm• Maximum rotation speed: 300 rpm• Maximum Syringe drive force: >=100 N• Fluid port: 1/4-28 UNF female• Syringe wash port: 10-32 UNF• Communication: RS-232 / RS-485• Baud rates: 9600 / 19200 / 38400 / 57600 / 115200 bps• Power supply: 24 VDC / 3 A for the integrated-driver version• Operating temperature: 5-55 C• Relative humidity: <=80% RH, non-condensing• Size with driver: approximately 44.5 x 62.3 x 153 mm• Size without driver: approximately 44.5 x 62.3 x 133.4 mm• Weight: approximately 0.46 kg with driver / 0.42 kg without driverApplications• Laboratory and analytical instruments• Online water-quality monitoring systems• Biochemical, blood, electrolyte and trace-element analyzers• Chromatographic and petroleum-testing instruments• Reagent sampling and micro-dosing modules• Automated filling and dispensing equipment• Custom OEM fluid-handling systems 
