water and water-treatment systems• Laboratory and analytical instruments• Reagent and sample fluid transfer• Chemical-processing and industrial fluid-control systems• Fluid paths used with syringe pumps, valves and rigid-tube fittingsPFA Tube Selection Notes• Select the inner diameter according to the required flow rate and internal volume.• Match the outer diameter to the receiving fitting and connection method.• Confirm fluid compatibility using the actual chemical, concentration, temperature and exposure time.• Confirm the allowable pressure for the selected tube size, temperature and fitting arrangement.• Specify whether flanging service is required when requesting a quotation.• Provide the required tube length or packaging format with the selected SKU or model number.Frequently Asked QuestionsWhat is PFA tube used for?PFA tube is used for transferring high-purity or chemically demanding fluids in semiconductor, ultrapure-water, laboratory, chemical-processing and analytical systems.What is the continuous-use temperature range?The stated continuous-use temperature range is -100°C to +260°C.Which PFA tube sizes are available?RUNZE offers 19 standard ID/OD combinations from 0.5 x 1.6 mm to 8.0 x 10.0 mm.Is the tubing transparent?Yes. The listed RUNZE PFA tubing is fully transparent for easier visual inspection of the fluid path.Can RUNZE provide flanged PFA tubing?Flanging service is available for the models marked Yes in the specification table.How should I choose a PFA tube model?Provide the required ID, OD, fluid, concentration, operating temperature, pressure, length and connection method so the matching model and fitting can be confirmed. 
